1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,750
A high confidence score does not show that a pose is right.

2
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:12,900
In published evaluations the best confidence metrics reach about 75 ROC AUC.

3
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,250
Given only the score, an LLM agent called all 12 perturbed Boltz-2 poses valid.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:22,600
The pockets were cut to glycine, so all of these poses are invalid.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,450
Six layers. The first three check the inputs before any model runs.

6
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:30,350
Layer three: does the model apply to this target?

7
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,000
Layers four and five check the outputs.

8
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:37,350
Each check returns pass, warn, stop or skip.

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,800
It records the evidence and the threshold, and says where the threshold comes from.

10
00:00:42,188 --> 00:00:51,308
New run: describe the run in plain words.

11
00:00:51,458 --> 00:00:58,773
Quick setup reads the request and looks up the target and ligand in UniProt, PubChem and RCSB.

12
00:00:58,923 --> 00:01:05,408
Tools can also be picked from the menu. Here AutoDock Vina is added.

13
00:01:05,558 --> 00:01:12,232
Start run. Executors are dispatched to Modal and checks stream into the log.

14
00:01:12,382 --> 00:01:15,732
Input checks report first. The GPU runs on Modal take longer.

15
00:01:15,882 --> 00:01:23,222
Jobs lists every run with its six layer bars and verdict.

16
00:01:23,372 --> 00:01:29,155
The report opens on the issues that limit the claim, each with its value and threshold.

17
00:01:29,305 --> 00:01:35,529
Ensemble lays out every structure in a run. This one holds the 3PTB reference.

18
00:01:36,029 --> 00:01:40,029
Each run renders up to 10 structures as PyMOL sessions and PNG files.

19
00:01:40,529 --> 00:01:45,129
report.html is written from the run record, with every value, threshold and origin.

20
00:01:45,629 --> 00:01:51,029
The provenance graph links sources, files, tools, checks and the verdict, with checksums.

21
00:01:51,529 --> 00:01:55,729
Figures for PoseBusters tests, seed spread and contacts come from the same record.

22
00:01:56,329 --> 00:02:00,279
Four systems, wild type and perturbed, on Boltz-2 and DiffDock-L (Modal A100).

23
00:02:00,429 --> 00:02:04,429
The agent judges each pose from the score, then from the fact file.

24
00:02:05,029 --> 00:02:08,979
Run 3: balanced accuracy 0.50 from the score, 0.75 with the fact file.

25
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:11,529
95% CI 0.50 to 1.0, McNemar p 0.125.

26
00:02:12,129 --> 00:02:15,779
With the fact file, the agent rejected all 12 perturbed Boltz-2 poses.

27
00:02:15,929 --> 00:02:18,629
It also rejected some valid poses, most often DiffDock-L.

28
00:02:19,129 --> 00:02:22,179
CDK2, pocket cut to glycine: ipTM 0.925, pocket pLDDT 82.3.

29
00:02:22,329 --> 00:02:26,529
It recovers 1 of 9 deposited contacts. The wild type recovers 6 of 9.

30
00:02:27,129 --> 00:02:29,279
371 Python tests and 203 web tests.

31
00:02:29,429 --> 00:02:33,029
An example with seven planted input faults gives seven stops.

